{"run": "digest", "t": 32123, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Gaza war — The United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs reports that dozens of children and civilians have been killed in Gaza including a medical storage facility."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32123, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Gaza war — The Israel Defense Forces says that they have killed two Hamas militants in separate airstrikes in central Gaza and the Shati camp in Gaza City respectively, including a Nukhba Force commander who took part in the October 7 attacks."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32123, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Red Sea crisis — Shipping data shows that two tanker ships carrying oil from Saudi Arabia, the Suezmax Malta-flagged Lesvos and the VLCC Desh Vaibhav, have exited the Red Sea through the Bab-el-Mandeb strait."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32123, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] At least fourteen people are killed in a series of floods in southern India."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32123, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Health and environment] 2026 European heatwaves — Italy experiences its fourth heatwave of the summer with the health ministry issuing red alerts for a record 25 cities."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32123, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] COVID-19 pandemic in Poland — Poland's Ministry of Health appeals a Brussels court ruling ordering the country to accept and pay approximately €1.3 billion for unwanted COVID-19 vaccine doses produced by Pfizer and BioNTech."}
